vaevictis-tools (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release, for systems installed from VaeVictis OS 1.1. Fixes found
    with AI-assisted reviews (not an independent security audit):
  * vv-sandbox: only regular files given as arguments, after following links;
    a file reached through a link is bound alone and read-only; hidden files,
    files in hidden folders and in ~/bin are read-only; nothing of /run (except
    /run/media), /proc, /sys or /dev; never a folder; secrets moved elsewhere
    behind a link are hidden at their real place; the program gets the
    resolved paths of the accepted files only.
  * vv-vpn-helper: "Table" other than auto and "FwMark" are refused (custom
    routing could leave the traffic outside the tunnel while it shows as
    connected); every [Peer] needs an Endpoint; the kill switch flag is
    root-only; disconnecting a tunnel never releases the kill switch of
    another one.
  * VPN polkit rule: the password is asked at every action (auth_admin).
  * v-snap: refuses a system snapshot or restore when /usr, /usr/local, /var
    or /var/lib are separate partitions; never copies or deletes another
    snapshot store.
  * vv-vpn, vv-panic, vv-panic-action: commands only from the system folders.

